WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.660
At the end of A Storm of Swords, and of Season
4, of Game of Thrones, Tywin Lannister is

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:12.370
killed by his son, Tyrion. But a popular theory
claims that Tywin is already dying, that he’s

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.699
poisoned, by Oberyn Martell.
So Oberyn Martell is the younger brother of

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:22.240
Doran Martell, the Prince of Dorne, and of
Elia Martell, who was murdered in Robert’s

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.509
Rebellion. Oberyn’s the father of eight
bastard daughters, called the “sand snakes”,

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:32.430
who he had with various women including Ellaria
Sand. Oberyn has a “fearsome” reputation

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.980
as a fighter and a lover. He’s travelled
the Free Cities, studied at the Citadel, and

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:42.650
soldiered in the Disputed Lands. Doran calls
him “Deadly, dangerous, unpredictable”.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:48.540
Tywin calls him “half-mad”. Varys says
he’s “a proud man”, and “sentimental”.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.920
Oberyn was close with his sister Elia, and,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.690
like the rest of his family, he is outraged
by her murder at the hands of Gregor Clegane.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:59.810
So when he comes to King’s Landing, Oberyn
makes clear that he comes for justice, not

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:05.100
just for Gregor, but for the man who gave
his orders, Tywin. He never says outright

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.899
that he wants to kill Tywin, but he hints
it heavily to Tyrion, telling him “Your

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:14.350
father … may not live forever”.
Oberyn’s known as a poisoner, having learned

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.450
the trade on his travels. In his fight with
Gregor Clegane, Oberyn uses a poisoned spear,

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.670
which is what kills Gregor after Oberyn’s
own death. He’s also rumoured to have used

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.770
a poisoned sword in a duel with Lord Edgar
Yronwood, back when Oberyn was sixteen. This

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:33.929
earned him the name Red Viper.
So we know Oberyn wants revenge on Tywin,

00:01:33.929 --> 00:01:39.469
and we know Oberyn uses poisons. Is there evidence
that Tywin is poisoned before he's killed

00:01:39.469 --> 00:01:43.850
by Tyrion? On the night of Tywin’s death,
Tyrion finds his father in the privy, which

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.539
some fans suggest shows that Tywin’s been
poisoned with “Widow’s blood … A [poison

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:52.969
mentioned by Pycelle that] shuts down a man’s
bladder and bowels, until he drowns in his

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:58.350
own poisons”. But – being on the toilet
doesn’t prove that you’ve been given constipation

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.909
poison, right? Especially considering Shae
is in Tywin’s bed at the time. Are we meant

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:06.819
to believe Tywin was in the mood while his
bowels were shut down and he was “drown[ing]

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:11.200
in his own poisons”? Others point to the
line saying that Tyrion “[finds] his father

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.000
where he knew he’d find him, seated in the
dimness of the privy tower”. But Tyrion

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.290
knows Tywin is there not because he knows
he’s on widow’s blood but because Tyrion

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:24.420
was just in Tywin’s bedroom, where he expected
to find him, and Tywin wasn’t there. So

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.310
Tywin being in the privy is not evidence
that he’s poisoned.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:33.019
But there is another thing. After Tywin’s
death, something weird and gross and wrong

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:38.489
goes on with his corpse, which is laid out
in the Sept of Baelor. The body rots, with

00:02:38.489 --> 00:02:44.099
greenish skin and leaking fluid, and it stinks,
so badly that Tommen retches, Pycelle’s

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:48.540
eyes water, and one of the Most Devout has
to be helped from the room. Davos hears

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.049
that the “corpse [stinks] so badly that
no one [is] able to enter the … Sept … for

00:02:52.049 --> 00:02:56.909
days afterward”. This isn’t meant to
happen. The room is filled with incense, and

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.590
silent sisters prepare the body, removing
bowls and organs, stuffing in “salts and

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:07.510
fragrant herbs”, yet Tywin’s body still
really stinks. What does this mean? There’s

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:12.549
a famous Russian book called The Brothers
Karamazov where a monk dies, and his body

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:16.420
stinks afterwards, shocking and upsetting
people, and making them think that the monk

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:21.349
was somehow corrupt or dishonest. So in the
same way, the stink of Tywin’s corpse might

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:26.230
mean he’s a rotten person. It might mean
that his murder by his son is terrible and

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:31.510
wrong, that his relationships with his family,
and his legacy are bad. And Tywin’s rotting,

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:37.750
smiling corpse is a “mockery” of his pride
and power and sternness in life. So the “horror”

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.069
of Tywin’s body means lots of things. Some
have suggested that it also shows that Tywin’s

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:48.480
body is corrupted by poison. But this doesn’t
actually make a whole lot of sense. If Tywin

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.469
is poisoned by Oberyn, it must happen before
Oberyn’s death in Tyrion X. The most likely

00:03:53.469 --> 00:03:58.379
time seems Jaime VII, when Tywin has breakfast
with Oberyn. But whenever it happens, there’s

00:03:58.379 --> 00:04:02.859
a good chunk of time between the poisoning
and Tywin’s death, so it seems really weird

00:04:02.859 --> 00:04:07.310
that Tywin is apparently totally unaffected
by the poison right up until he’s dead when

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:12.730
it suddenly makes his body gross. It is plausible
that Oberyn could use some slow-acting poison,

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.919
but it’s pretty implausible that the poison
would only happen to kick in right after Tywin’s

00:04:16.919 --> 00:04:22.520
death, and its only effects are decomposition
and ickiness that can happen naturally anyway.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:25.810
So, especially considering that the “horror”
of Tywin’s corpse already means a bunch

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:30.310
of stuff, it doesn’t seem to have anything
to do with poison.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.300
One other thing to consider – Doran, Oberyn’s
brother, says that he’s been “work[ing]

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.449
at the downfall of Tywin Lannister since [Robert’s
Rebellion]”, hoping to “strip [Tywin]

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:42.360
of all that he [holds] most dear before”
killing him, so he’s disappointed when

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:47.460
Tyrion kills Tywin – Doran doesn’t want
Tywin dead yet. This is important, because

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.520
Doran says that he works closely with Oberyn
in their plans to strike at their enemies.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.240
If they’re working closely together, Oberyn
would surely share Doran’s goal of “stripping

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.250
[Tywin] of all that he [holds] most dear before”
killing him, so he wouldn’t kill him right

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:05.259
after arriving at King’s Landing. It’s
true that Oberyn’s impatient, unpredictable,

00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:10.180
“bloodthirsty”, even. But would a bloodthirsty
man secretly and anonymously kill his enemy

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.560
with a slow-acting poison? Look at how Oberyn
kills Gregor – he makes a show of it, demands

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:20.810
a public confession, insists on killing Gregor
with his own hands. It’s not at all Oberyn’s

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:27.710
style to quietly poison Tywin, and it probably
goes against Doran and Oberyn’s plans.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:32.710
So at first glance, it seems totally reasonable
to think that Oberyn might poison Tywin. Oberyn

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:36.720
wants revenge on Tywin, Oberyn’s known to
use poison, the two even have a convenient

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.360
breakfast together not long before Tywin’s
death. But the closer you look at this theory,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.620
the less sense it makes. Oberyn’s known
to use poisoned weapons in duels, but slipping

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.440
poison into peoples’ morning tea is not
his style at all. Slow-acting poison, too,

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:55.060
which apparently has no effect on Tywin in
the time between Oberyn’s death and his.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.270
Tywin’s being on the privy and the stench
of his corpse have more to do with subverting

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:04.240
his dignity and reputation than with any exotic
poison. At the end of the day, while it is

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.419
possible that Oberyn poisons Tywin, there's no evidence that it happens, and there

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:12.520
are good reasons to believe that it probably
doesn’t. So the most reasonable conclusion

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.219
is that Oberyn did not poison Tywin.
Thanks for watching.

